<article class="env-remark" id="07IC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07IC">Remark <span data-tag="07IC">60.8.5</span> <span class="named">(Functoriality)</span>.</a>  Let $p$ be a prime number. Let $(S, \mathcal{I}, \gamma ) \to (S', \mathcal{I}', \gamma ')$ be a morphism of divided power schemes over $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$. Set $S_0 = V(\mathcal{I})$ and $S'_0 = V(\mathcal{I}')$. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[r]_ f \ar[d] &  Y \ar[d] \\  S_0 \ar[r] &  S'_0 }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes and assume $p$ is locally nilpotent on $X$ and $Y$. Then we get a continuous and cocontinuous functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{CRIS}(X/S) \longrightarrow \text{CRIS}(Y/S')  \]
</div>
  <p> by letting $(U, T, \delta )$ correspond to $(U, T, \delta )$ with $U \to X \to Y$ as the $S'$-morphism from $U$ to $Y$. Hence we get a morphism of topoi </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f_{\text{CRIS}} : (X/S)_{\text{CRIS}} \longrightarrow (Y/S')_{\text{CRIS}}  \]
</div>
  <p> see Sites, Section <a href="/tag/00XN" data-tag="00XN">7.21</a>. </p>
</article>